1.4.0 (2026-11-28):
- Examples and README: MQTT topics afya/… instead of librus/… (afya/jas/dane, afya/dane, afya/sms/json, afya/sms/tekst)
- Grades page: default path afya/oceny (was librus); help, README and examples use afya/<child>,
  e.g. afya/jas – existing nodes keep the path they have
- Default SMS templates start with the student (%uczen%: …) instead of "Librus %uczen%: …";
  nodes with their own template are not affected
- Examples: librus-sms rebuilt – two children, schedule, new grade and new note as separate SMS
  (switches on payload.tekstOceny / payload.tekstUwagi), one function per phone number, HTTP SMS gateway
  with a token header, full result to MQTT; librus-mqtt – new grade and new note handled separately
- Edit dialog: new setting "Labels" – descriptions in Polish for a Polish system, English for all others,
  or chosen by hand (English / Polski); only the descriptions change, fields and values stay the same

1.3.0 (2026-11-28):
- Separate texts: payload.tekstOceny (new grades) and payload.tekstUwagi (new notes), each with its own template;
  payload.tekst still holds both together (grades, then notes) – existing flows keep working
- Edit dialog: "New grade" and "New note" sections, each with its own checkbox on top –
  "Send info about a new grade" (new, on by default; older nodes stay on) and "Send info about a new note"
  (was "Also read teacher notes", same setting); "Without Polish letters" applies to both texts
- msg.test reports only the kinds that are switched on
- Grades page: a small date (month.day, without the year) under every grade – no need to hover;
  hover / tap still shows the full details

1.2.0 (2026-11-25):
- Grades page: access token – the link ...?token=... opens the page without logging in (smart mirror,
  wall tablet); "Generate" and "Copy" buttons in the edit dialog; the token works with or without a password
- Grades page: own page title (header and browser tab; empty = student's name)
- Wrong tokens count like wrong passwords (10 tries in 15 minutes, then the address is blocked for a while)

1.1.0 (2026-11-25):
- New (optional): the last result is also stored in a global/flow context variable
- Edit dialog and node status in English, help and README in English + Polish
- New: grades page served by the node (path + password per node, e.g. /librus/john): class, subjects A–Z,
  weighted average after the subject name, grades with date / category / weight on hover, terms and whole year,
  mobile and dark mode
- Averages taken from Librus (columns Śr.I / Śr.II / Śr.R); calculated from the Librus weights only where the
  school hides them; new year average "R" and payload.srednieLibrus
- Output fields and SMS templates otherwise unchanged
- New modern edit dialog (sections, live summary, spinners, validation), palette category "AFYA",
  Font Awesome icon, English UI with English + Polish help
- Short, consistent node status (value · time)
- MIT license, Node-RED >= 3.0, Node.js >= 18, unit tests (`npm test`)

1.0.0:
- first version: grades, teacher notes, SMS text, MQTT example
